📘 Rich Dad’s Guide to Financial Freedom — Robert T. Kiyosaki
🔹 1500-Word Informative Summary

Rich Dad’s Guide to Financial Freedom is a practical roadmap for people who want to escape the “rat race” and achieve financial independence. Robert Kiyosaki explains that financial freedom is not about earning more salary—it is about building assets that generate passive income.

The book continues the philosophy introduced in Rich Dad Poor Dad. Kiyosaki contrasts two mindsets:

Poor/Middle-Class Mindset: Work for money, depend on salary, save little, rely on job security.

Rich Mindset: Make money work for you, build assets, invest wisely, focus on long-term freedom.

What Is Financial Freedom?

Financial freedom means your passive income (from businesses, real estate, investments) is greater than your living expenses. When this happens, you no longer need to work for money—you work because you want to, not because you have to.

